## Review Scope
Judge only what this change is responsible for. When a proof fails because of a test or code the change did not touch, confirm it also fails on a clean main, then verdict that criterion with failure_class=UNRELATED_FAILURE (or ENVIRONMENTAL for broken tooling) rather than FAIL for the worker to rework. When the work session cites commit SHAs, check they are on the branch under review before crediting them, and if they are not, use failure_class=WRONG_BRANCH.

## Instructions
Evaluate every acceptance criterion against the diff above. Also verify the implementation follows the plan (if provided).
Output ONLY a single JSON object with no surrounding text:
{"overall":"PASS","summary":"concise assessment","verdicts":[{"criterion_index":0,"outcome":"PASS","evidence":"direct quote from diff"}]}
Optional per-verdict fields failure_class and proposed_waiver: For each criterion that is not PASS, set failure_class so the app routes it correctly: NOT_DONE (default) when the worker has more to do. CANNOT_VERIFY when you lack access to the evidence. UNRELATED_FAILURE when the proof fails only because of a test or code the change did not touch. ENVIRONMENTAL when tooling, network, or CI outside the change is broken. WRONG_BRANCH when the cited commits are not on the reviewed branch. UNATTAINABLE when the criterion cannot be met as written. Anything except NOT_DONE goes to the owner instead of another rework round, so use it only when more work in this change cannot fix the gap. When you judge the owner should waive the criterion, also set proposed_waiver=true and put the reason in evidence.

Valid outcome values: PASS, FAIL, PARTIAL, UNVERIFIABLE. Mark a criterion UNVERIFIABLE rather than guessing if you cannot confirm it from what's in front of you — a missing or incomplete diff is a known limitation of this mode, not a signal the work is wrong.
